  "body": "### Summary\nAs the maintainer, I want the offline page saving removed from SwiftHFR, as it was removed from the legacy app, because it was rarely used and costly to maintain.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (validated legacy parity, ROADMAP). Source: operator UI comparison of 2026-11-11, side-by-side simulator captures 09 (pseudos redacted, attached below when available).\n\n### Context\n- Operator decision, 2026-11-11: the feature was removed from legacy for low use and maintenance cost.\n- SwiftHFR ships it: \"Enregistrer cette page hors ligne\" in the reader's \"⋯\" (LOT-068 #93, LOT-139 #229, both closed); GAP-180 still lists it as parity.\n\n### To decide (operator)\n1. Hide the entry only, or remove the feature and its storage.\n2. Pages already saved by testers: delete them at launch, or keep them readable until the next release (AGENTS persistence rule: data written by a released version stays readable; TestFlight builds count?).\n\n### Scope once decided\n- Remove the menu entry and every other entry point (list, settings).\n- Remove or retire the code and storage per point 1–2, with a migration if needed.\n- Update GAP-180 and LOTS.md (LOT-068, LOT-139) through the PR's `### Ledger` section.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
